on  so what are you saying maybe by by april  by may  april is pretty realistic for this kind  of a number  but uh it will depend a lot on  no offensement but what is referred to  as british  mutation we are suffering from it right  now  uh here and there is no reason  in the world to believe that the vaccine  is not  working vis-a-vis these new mutations  but it definitely influences the numbers  you believe that the rise in the spike  in cases in  israel is largely down to the british  mutation do you  i can't say largely due to but  uh we think this is part of the problem  we found cases here in israel  some of them by the way  directed straight to people coming from  from britain in the recent weeks  some of some of them people who have no  connection whatsoever to  to england or or traveling abroad or  anything of the kind so  unfortunately it's here we do have to  say for a fact that is here  when you were talking just now about the  vaccine you had a broad smile on your  face  you must be one of very few uh health  ministers around the wing governments  around the world  with a smile on their face at the moment  and what advice do you give  to countries around the world who are  really struggling  with the vaccination program  well first of all uh it's difficult to  smile broadly when we have these numbers  of newly infected so i  i guess half of my face is smiling the  other half is still  this still has a worried expression on  it but  uh in terms of the uh advice  i would say what i already mentioned  during our conversation  get out there don't don't put a huge  station in the middle of the of your  cabin  and wait for people to come especially  when you're talking about population  interest  try to get it out to if not to their  homes then at least to their  areas to their suburbs to their towns  probably  probably it will help many other  countries i spoke to some of my  colleagues including  including the british minister of health  i think that  every